{
  "title": "Comprehensive Dua for this World & the Hereafter",
  "data": "After the dawn (fajr) prayer, recite 10 times (or keep reciting it until sunrise):\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ الْعَظيْمِ وَبِحَمْدِهٖ اَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ وَاَسْئَلُهٗ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHIL A’ZEEME WA BE-HAMDEHI ASTAGHFERUL LAAHA WA AS-ALOHu MIN FAZLEHI.\nGlory be to Allah, the Great, and by His praise; I seek forgiveness from Allah and I ask Him of His bounty.",
  "merits": "Ahmad ibn Fahad and others have reported that a man came to Imam Abul Hasan al-Kazim (a.s.) and complained about his profession and that whenever he went to do any of his affairs, it would not be settled. The Imam (a.s.) advised him to repeat this dhikr ten times after the dawn (fajr) prayer.\n\nThe man then said, “A little time after I had committed myself to this instruction, people from the desert came to me to inform that one of my relatives had died and he had no inheritor except me. I therefore went there to receive the inheritance due to which I became rich.”\n\nQuoted from the two books of al-Kafi and Makarim al-Akhlaq: A man, called Halqam, asked the Holy Imam (a.s.) to teach him a brief supplicatory utterance by which the wealth of this world and the goodness of the Hereafter are gathered to him. The Imam (a.s.) therefore instructed him to repeat this supplicatory utterance after the dawn (fajr) prayer up to sunrise. When the man did, his conditions were changed excellently."
}
